<title>USA: Essex Q1 shr loss vs profit after gain.</title>
<headline>Essex Q1 shr loss vs profit after gain.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBIA, Md. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>ESSEX CORPORATION</p>
<p>			FOR THE THIRTEEN WEEK PERIODS ENDED</p>
<p>					  Mar 30, 1997     Mar 31, 1996</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>Technical Services/</p>
<p>    Products			    $2,868,000	 $3,774,000</p>
<p>Optoelectronic</p>
<p>    Products/Services		    679,000	    471,000</p>
<p>	Total				3,547,000	  4,245,000</p>
<p>Operating Income (Loss):</p>
<p>Technical Services/</p>
<p>    Products				(44,000)	    150,000</p>
<p>Optoelectronic</p>
<p>   Products/Services		   (362,000)	  (756,000)</p>
<p>	Total				(406,000)	  (606,000)</p>
<p> Income (Loss) Before Taxes	  (459,000)	  1,325,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)		     (459,000)	  1,071,000</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of  </p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding		  3,626,000	  3,593,000</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per Share:</p>
<p>   Primary				    (0.13)		 0.30</p>
<p> Fully Diluted				(0.13)		 0.28</p>
<p> Working Capital (Deficit)	   (293,000)	  2,524,000</p>
<p> Working Capital Ratio		    0.92:1	     1.65:1</p>
<p> Stockholders' Equity		    273,000	  3,131,000</p>
<p>NOTE: Net income in the 1996 first quarter resulted from a gain on settlement of a lawsuit after attorneys' fees and related expenses of about $1,722,000 or $0.48 per share. Excluding these items, results from operations would have produced a net loss of $651,000, or $0.18. The per share results are computed on weighted average shares outstanding of 3,626,000 in 1997 and 3,593,000 in 1996.</p>
</text>
